<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Apries</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 589–570 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Wahibre</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Apries was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of the 26th Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, reigning from 589 to 570 BCE. He intervened in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> and sent an army against the Greek colony of Cyrene, whose defeat at Irasa around 570 BCE provoked a mutiny. The general Amasis was proclaimed king in his place, and Apries was later killed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/apries.jpg" alt="Apries" width="199" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: de:Benutzer:Kl833x9; de:Benutzer:Daniel FR · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apries.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
